 ### 16.17 Jiang scorecard update
 #39 (JIANG CALL, 0.60: by 8/31 Brent >100 AND a global food/inflation emergency dominates) resolved MISS: the oil leg printed (100.69 close on 7/23, one session) but the FAO food index was +2.5pct y/y and July CPI was +0.1 m/m - no emergency. His DIRECTION on oil was right and EARLY (Brent 101-109 came 9/9-9/15, after his window); his MAGNITUDE-and-cascade timing was wrong. Consistent with 14 (limitations): take his direction and chokepoint salience, never his clock. Jiang-seed rows: 1 resolved, Brier 0.36.
 
+### 16.18 Forecast the cycle's DURATIONS, LEVELS and MARKERS - never the direction of the next leg (2026-09-20 research review)
+16.15 found the error (0-for-8 extrapolating the live leg). This section says what to forecast INSTEAD, and it is not 'the opposite leg': a gate that flips an escalation bias into a de-escalation bias repeats the error with the sign changed (Chang, Berdini, Mandel & Tetlock 2018 on one-directional debiasing). What the conflict literature finds forecastable:
+- THE LEVEL PERSISTS, THE DIRECTION DOES NOT. In the ViEWS prediction competitions (Vesco et al. 2022; Hegre et al. 2024) every country-month model lost to the no-change baseline on the change metric, and a country's own last 12 months used as the forecast DISTRIBUTION was a strong benchmark. That distribution contains both legs. The engine extrapolated the first difference; the evidence backs extrapolating the level.
+- A TALKS ROUND IS NEAR-NEUTRAL FOR TERMINATION. Min (2020), daily data on every interstate war since 1816: after 1945 negotiations are more frequent and 'far less predictive of war termination'. Islamabad, Doha, a new list of conditions - none of these moves a termination probability by itself. What moves it is below.
+- THIS PAUSE SITS IN THE WORST DURABILITY CELL. Fortna (2003), 48 interstate ceasefires 1946-97, 21 resumed: hazard after a stalemate ~27x that after a decisive outcome; sharply lower with a demilitarized zone, monitors, or a third-party guarantee; a formal agreement ALONE was not significant. Werner & Yuen (2005): ceasefires imposed by outside pressure before the battlefield was clear fail more. Beardsley (2008): mediated deals hold short-run and decay as the mediator's leverage fades. (Table values read by machine - check the PDF before quoting.)
+- SORT THE OBSTACLE FIRST. If the fight is about INFORMATION (relative strength), fighting reveals it, positions converge, swings damp (Slantchev 2003). If it is a COMMITMENT problem (enrichment, sanctions sequencing, who moves first), fighting reveals nothing that helps, pauses are tactical, and the cycle runs until the balance changes or a guarantee appears. Ask after every leg: did it reveal anything new? If not, expect another talk-fight turn, not a trend.
+THE RULE (mandatory for cluster iran-war; R27 in pipeline/schema.py): no row whose content is 'the next leg goes this way'. Use one of four shapes, each with its own pricing anchor:
+1. DURATION - 'the current pause (or round) lasts beyond D' / 'ends by D'. Priced by `python tools/cycle_odds.py --completed <past phase lengths> --current <age> --days <to horizon>`: the cycle's own phase lengths pulled toward a reference class. Quote the BAND. A P more than 0.10 outside it is a view and needs a dated, capital-committed catalyst (a deployment order, a deadline with teeth), never the tone of the day's headlines. Pauses so far: Jun-17 -> Jul-7 (20d), ~Jul-30 -> Aug-31 (32d); the Apr-8 -> Apr-22 pause (14d) ended in a blockade rather than strikes - include it only when the row counts a blockade as an ending.
+2. MARKER - 'a monitoring mechanism / DMZ-equivalent / third-party guarantee / signed text is announced by D'. These are Fortna's observable durability markers and the ONLY things that justify moving frozen-conflict or the termination nodes materially. Base rate: one signed text (Jun-17) in ~7 months of war, zero monitors or guarantees - so low single digits to ~0.2 over a 6-week window depending on the marker. When a marker appears, lengthen --prior-median in cycle_odds (193d is the 100-fatality-threshold median in Clayton et al. 2022; 65d is the default).
+3. PHYSICAL LEVEL - 'Hormuz transits below X pct of pre-war on D', 'Saudi exports below Y'. A repaired facility recovers in days (Abqaiq 2019); traffic through a THREATENED chokepoint stays depressed long after attacks stop (Suez ~60pct below 2023 after ~100 quiet days, secondary source). This is where the 8-for-8 came from.
+4. INVARIANT - true in both the escalation and the mediation world (16.15).
+PRICING DISCIPLINE: every such row still carries the outside-view reference (--base-rate/--base-class; the cycle_odds band IS the base rate for a duration row), and is looked at again every session (`ledger.py stale` -> `revise` in small dated steps or `confirm`). The next-leg node in data/timelines.json is priced from cycle_odds, not from the headlines, and 'US strikes resume' can never be priced above 'the pause ends'.
